# This file contains the list of files and directories that should be ignored by Git.
# Because this is a JavaScript project, we are ignoring the node_modules directory, the dist directory, and the .parcel-cache directory.
# * The node_modules directory contains all the dependencies of the project, which can be installed using npm install.       
# * The dist directory contains the compiled code that is generated by Parcel when building the project.
# * The .parcel-cache directory contains the cache files generated by Parcel, which can be safely ignored.
# * The .gitignore file is used to prevent certain files and directories from being tracked by Git.

# Since they can re generated from the source code, they are not necessary to be included in the repository.
#  *This helps to keep the repository clean and reduces the size of the repository.
